  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "Which of the following is equivalent to “If \\(P\\) is true then \\(Q\\) is false”?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "“\\(P\\) is true or \\(Q\\) is false.”"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "“If \\(Q\\) is false then \\(P\\) is true.”"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "“If \\(P\\) is false then \\(Q\\) is true.”"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "“If \\(Q\\) is true then \\(P\\) is false.”"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "“If \\(Q\\) is true then \\(P\\) is true.”"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1974-p13.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The contrapositive of “\\(P\\) true implies \\(Q\\) false” is “\\(Q\\) not false implies \\(P\\) not true.” This is exactly “If \\(Q\\) is true then \\(P\\) is false.”\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
      "hints": [
        "An implication is equivalent to its contrapositive",
        "Reverse the implication and negate both “\\(P\\) true” and “\\(Q\\) false”"
      ],
